    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm hitting a massive headache with our jenkins pipeline. we've got these intermittent failures during the unit test stage in our CI/CD flow. the code hasn't changed, but the builds are just... flaky. sometimes it passes, sometimes it fails with weird timeout errors or random asset loading failures. it's non-deterministic as hell. how can i start isolating whether this is an env issue or something in the container orchestration?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Flaky tests in Jenkins, especially with timeouts and asset loading issues, are a classic sign of environmental instability. You should start by checking the resource allocation for your build agents—are they being starved of CPU or memory? If your container orchestration is running the tests, inspect the container logs for resource throttling warnings. Sometimes, a simple race condition on shared network resources within the container environment can mimic a code bug.",
      "source": "target",
