    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i checked the resource usage and it seems like the agents have plenty of headroom. the weird thing is the timing. it feels totally random. like it's just some glitch in the system that comes and goes. is there a specific way to log these things more granularly so i can see if it's actually a network hiccup or just the build environment being unstable? i'm trying to rule out everything before i start refactoring the test suite itself.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the resource headroom is fine, you'll need to increase the verbosity of your logging significantly. Try enabling debug logging within your testing framework itself, not just the Jenkins agent logs. You might also want to introduce artificial, small delays (like `sleep` calls) strategically between critical test steps to see if the failure pattern changes. This can help distinguish between a genuine timing issue and a subtle environmental stutter.",
      "source": "target",
